From 77f065bcc607f915638147fd4c2e13dfc5d29740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:09:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the television depth shaders out of Visual Studio's
 shader compiler

The Visual Studio generator hands every .hlsl file in a target's sources to
FXC, with entry point main and the project's default profile.
ScreenDepthComposite.hlsl has two entry points (VSMain, PSMain) and is not
compiled at build time at all: ScreenDepthPass compiles it at start-up from the
text ScreenDepthShaderSource.hpp embeds. Listed in Open77.Client's sources it
failed the build:

    FXC : error X3501: 'main': entrypoint not found

The two shader files stay where they are, beside the header that carries them,
and Open77.ScreenDepthShaderSource.Tests still fails while the three disagree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qum3jofThN9KuYZN8xcYdD
---
 client/CMakeLists.txt | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/client/CMakeLists.txt b/client/CMakeLists.txt
index 0fa3c02c..152fdf1b 100644
--- a/client/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/client/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1297,8 +1297,8 @@ target_sources(
         src/webui/SceneDepth.hpp
         src/webui/SceneDepthPolicy.hpp
         src/webui/ScreenDepth.hpp
-        src/webui/ScreenDepth.hlsli
-        src/webui/ScreenDepthComposite.hlsl
+        # Not ScreenDepth.hlsli and ScreenDepthComposite.hlsl: Visual Studio would hand
+        # them to FXC. They are compiled at start-up from ScreenDepthShaderSource.hpp.
         src/webui/ScreenDepthPass.cpp
         src/webui/ScreenDepthPass.hpp
         src/webui/ScreenDepthShaderSource.hpp
-- 
